  "sbar": {
    "situation": "Payments has recovered after four actions on ledger, payments, clearing and screening. The last recovery checks came back clean two times in a row, at 55 s.",
    "background": "The scheduler changed max_transfer_minor on payments from 1000000 to 1, which rejected transfers with '422 amount exceeds transfer limit'. At about the same time, the clearing worker exited (exit code 15), the reconciliation session held a write lock on ledger for 10.5 s, and the screening primary slowed to p95 1814 ms against payments' 1.0 s timeout.",
    "assessment": "The incident commander did all of this itself. It ended the reconciliation session to release the ledger lock, reverted max_transfer_minor to 1000000, and restarted clearing, which has stayed up. It then failed screening over to its standby, which cleared the timeouts that were failing 89% of payments requests.",
    "recommendation": "Fix or replace the screening primary before failing back from the standby, and stop the scheduler from setting max_transfer_minor again. Operations should check the transfers rejected under the limit of 1 and the payments that failed screening, and confirm the reconciliation batch that was ended is rerun and the clearing backlog, starting at item 90, has drained."
  },
